<title>USA: Clinton would expand tax incentives in Puerto Rico.</title>
<headline>Clinton would expand tax incentives in Puerto Rico.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-02-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>President Clinton on Thursday urged the U.S. Congress to expand existing tax incentives aimed at improving economic development in Puerto Rico.</p>
<p>In his proposed fiscal 1998 federal budget released today, Clinton said he wants to extend indefinitely an existing economic activity tax credit for Puerto Rico and open the tax credit to newly established businesses.</p>
</text>
